<section class="idea-section not-content" aria-labelledby="guide-structure-title">
  <div class="idea-container">
    <header class="idea-intro">
      <h2 id="guide-structure-title">One system, studied in order</h2>
      <p>
        Agentic AI combines models with software components that hold context, call tools, preserve state, and produce side effects. The guide treats that whole system as the subject.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="guide-passes">
      <section>
        <h3>Build the functional model</h3>
        <p>Begin with software foundations, agent behavior, orchestration patterns, and the components used in complete agentic systems.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h3>Study security in context</h3>
        <p>Map threats, boundaries, controls, and tests back to the same components and workflows instead of learning them as an isolated checklist.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <p class="evidence-note">
      Chapters are grounded in official specifications and primary research, with local diagrams and minimal runnable examples where they help.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

